insight_1:
```markdown
Lower prices can generate high sales volumes when competition is stiff, but may negatively affect the perceived value of the product;
Raising prices above the competition during specific periods of low demand might help improve profit margins without significant market share loss;
Continuous monitoring and analysis of competitor strategies is essential to ensure optimal pricing decisions.
```

